# Energy balance with traveling pseudopotentials (A^nl term).
# Isolated Ne atom (PseudoDojo PBE v0.4 standard Ne.psp8), ground state at rest,
# then suddenly set moving at constant velocity v = 0.5 a.u. along x
# (atoms_dyn IMPULSIVE, traveling_pseudo ON); the electrons start at rest and
# slosh around the moving nucleus.
#
# With velocity-dependent projectors, the energy put in by the agent that keeps
# v constant is Delta(E_KS + A^nl.v) = v . Delta(P), where
#   A^nl = i<[V_nl, r]> = -dE_nl/dv   (nonlocal part of the electron momentum)
#   P    = d<sum r>/dt = <p> + A^nl  (physical electron momentum)
# (Stengel, Royo, Artacho, PRL 136, 196401 (2026), Eq. 6; see etf_kb.md).
# E_KS alone misses v . Delta(A^nl): a spurious oscillation.
# The checks are done by anl_check.sh from the printed energies, A^nl, the
# electronic current (<p>) and the electronic dipole computed from the density
# (P = -d dipole/dt; density_dipole ON). The atom starts at the box centre so
# that its density stays far from the cell boundaries.
# The cutoff must be converged (80 Ry): the relation P = <p> + A^nl assumes a
# complete basis; at 40 Ry it is off by about 0.1 (see etf_kb.md, section 12).
#
# 1) ground state with the atom at rest
set cell 14 0 0 0 14 0 0 0 14 bohr
species neon Ne.psp8
atom Ne neon 7.0 7.0 7.0 bohr 0.5 0.0 0.0 atomicvelocity
set xc PBE
set ecut 80 rydberg
set ecutprec 4 rydberg
set force_complex_wf ON
set wf_dyn PSDA
set wf_diag T
set threshold_scf 1.E-10 5
randomize_wf
run 0 100 5

# 2) sudden start at constant velocity; dipole printed at every step
set atoms_dyn IMPULSIVE
set traveling_pseudo ON
set wf_dyn ETRS
set density_dipole ON
set TD_dt 0.025 atomictime
set dt 0.025 atomictime
run 42 1
